        <h1>LeetCode 2243: Calculate Digit Sum of a String (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given a string s consisting of digits and an integer k. A round can be completed if
                the length of s is greater than k. In one round, do the following: divide s into consecutive
                groups of size k such that the first k characters are in the first group, the next k
                characters are in the second group, and so on (the size of the last group may be smaller
                than k); replace each group of s with a string representing the sum of all its digits; and
                merge consecutive groups together to form a new string. Repeat rounds until the length of s
                is less than or equal to k. Return s after all rounds have been completed.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: s = "11111222223", k = 3<br>
                Output: "135"<br>
                Explanation: In the first round, the groups are "111", "112", "222", and "23", which are
                replaced by "3", "4", "6", and "5", giving "3465". In the second round, the groups are "346"
                and "5", which are replaced by "13" and "5", giving "135". Since the length is now at most
                k, the answer is "135".
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    string digitSum(string s, int k) {
        while (s.size() &gt; k) {
            string res;
            for (int i = 0; i &lt; s.size(); i += k) {
                int sum = 0;
                for (int j = i; j &lt; s.size() &amp;&amp; j &lt; i + k; j++)
                    sum += s[j] - '0';
                res += to_string(sum);
            }
            s = res;
        }
        return s;
    }
};</code></pre>
